+# Audit 0.17.0: where the baby slept, and T.I.C.K.S.
+
+Method: design review only (detector not applicable, native platform): impeccable critique and
+graphic-design-fundamentals §13, on `today_sleeping_in_the_sling_light`, `patterns_places_ptBR_light`,
+`ticks_sheet_light`.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals §13
+
+| # | Check | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | Sling and arms naps seen without guilt; safe babywearing at the right moment. ✅ |
+| 2 | Concept | The brand's subject, in the data. ✅ |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | "Where" sits under the timer, above the one action. ✅ |
+| 4 | Contrast | Unpicked chips on the night panel were white pills (too heavy); now outlines in `on-panel-muted` with `on-panel` text. ✅ after fix |
+| 5 | Alignment | Chips wrap on the card's axis. ✅ |
+| 6 | Spacing | Tokens. ✅ |
+| 7 | Typography | Existing roles; T.I.C.K.S. rows are label + one meta line. ✅ |
+| 8 | Colour | Teal only on Woke up / Got it. ✅ |
+| 9 | Consistency | Same filter chips, a dark variant. ✅ |
+| 10 | Simplicity | Five places; the check shows once. ✅ |
+| 11 | Real size | Phone width, EN and PT. ✅ |
+| 12 | Accessibility | Chips are radio buttons; the check is plain text. ✅ |
+| 13 | Production | No migration (kind text); no new permission. ✅ |
+
+Safety: the T.I.C.K.S. text says the parent watches the baby, never the app (AAP 2022 rule).
+
+## impeccable critique
+
+| # | Heuristic | Score | Note |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | System status | 4 | The place is visible while asleep. |
+| 2 | Real world | 4 | "In arms", "Car seat", "No colo", "Cadeirinha". |
+| 3 | Control | 4 | One tap to change, also in the sheet. |
+| 4 | Consistency | 4 | Remembered like every other kind. |
+| 5 | Error prevention | n/a | |
+| 6 | Recognition | 4 | Words, the last one picked. |
+| 7 | Efficiency | 4 | Zero extra taps when the place is the same. |
+| 8 | Aesthetic | 4 | Calm on the panel after the fix. |
+| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | Change it any time. |
+| 10 | Help | 4 | T.I.C.K.S. when it matters, once. |
+| | **Total** | **35/36** | |
